  "initial_reflection": {
    "summary": "The run suffered severe HP attrition, falling from 80 HP to 18 HP by floor 6 and then to 3 HP after the Lagavulin fight. The final Slaver combat contained a clear survival error: the agent continued attacking while at 3 HP and facing an attack, instead of using the legal Defend. The deck also added Fire Breathing without any status or curse cards in the final build, giving it limited demonstrated synergy.",
    "lessons": [
      {
        "category": "COMBAT",
        "title": "At critical HP, block when the attack is not lethal",
        "situation": "When at very low HP, the enemy has an attack intent, and the current attack will not kill it.",
        "lesson": "Preserve survival over incremental damage: at the final Slaver decision, use Defend rather than Strike when Strike leaves the enemy alive and Defend is legal.",
        "evidence_points": [
          "At 3 HP, with the Slaver at 17 HP and Intent ATTACK, the legal alternatives included both Play Defend and Play Strike.",
          "The chosen Strike left the Slaver alive at 8/49 HP, so it was not a lethal attack."
        ],
        "reasoning": "Because the attack did not end the combat, spending the final energy on Strike provided damage without removing the immediate threat, while Defend was explicitly available at that state. This is a reusable threshold rule for low-HP turns.",
        "confidence": "high"
      },
      {
        "category": "CARD_REWARD",
